  "overview": {
    "id": "overview",
    "x": 108,
    "y": 80,
    "width": 1400,
    "height": 150,
    "layer": -3,
    "movable": false,
    "movableInEdit": false,
    "css": {
      "font-size": "25px"
    },
    "html": "Every function that works on widgets reads them from the same two parameters. <b>target</b> names the widgets themselves, <b>holder</b> names widgets whose <i>content</i> is meant &ndash; for a seat that is what lies in its hand and belongs to its player. Both accept either a list of widget ids or the name of a <b>collection</b> an earlier function filled, so it no longer matters which of the two the function before produced. If both are given, holder wins. Put a button into edit mode and press ctrl-j to read the routine behind it."
  },
